 "title": "Saccharomyces cerevisiae and Drosophila melanogaster Research Network",
 "summary": "This cluster revolves around research on Saccharomyces cerevisiae and Drosophila melanogaster, two organisms studied in various contexts. Oksana Tehlivets is involved in the conceptualization of S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine and the methodology of Saccharomyces cerevisiae. Gao Xiaoli and Zhang Shengwei contribute to the data curation and formal analysis of Saccharomyces cerevisiae, respectively. Drosophila melanogaster is investigated by Oksana Tehlivets, and its writing is attributed to Jutta Hafner. The research involves various methods, including Genomics, Proteomics, and Oxidative stress, which is linked to Apoptosis. The European Union funds the A4L_BRIDGE project, and Kohl JB studies H2S metabolism.",
